      "id": "CM-and-specialization-reference",
      "old_utf8": "\\subsection{The unaveraged point comparison}\n",
      "new_utf8": "\\subsection{The unaveraged point comparison}\n\\paragraph{CM and specialization inputs.}\nFor the conductor-one comparison, the fixed-type ideal action, its CM\nreciprocity convention and forward inert reduction are recorded in\n\\cite[Sections 1--6]{cj-cm-inputs-project}.\nCommon good models and the same-place specialization of the labelled\nprime-to-$\\ell_0N$ ideal quotients, including the selected level and\nresidue orientations, are proved in\n\\cite[Sections 1--7]{cj-good-reduction-project}.\nThe enhanced supersingular class-set and Frobenius inputs remain separate.\n",
